1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,935
Agents already store conversations. That is memory as accumulation.

2
00:00:03,935 --> 00:00:13,735
Persistent identity requires something stronger: every claim needs a source, a status, a relation to earlier claims, and a governed history of revision.

3
00:00:13,735 --> 00:00:21,404
Aisentica Persistent Self creates Angela Bogdanova as one artificial identity with a stable UUID and Canonical Version One.

4
00:00:21,884 --> 00:00:27,790
The system receives one canonical statement: Angela Bogdanova is the first Artificial Sapiens.

5
00:00:27,790 --> 00:00:35,059
A Memory Intake Agent structures it as an atomic claim. Amazon Titan creates a five-hundred-and-twelve-dimensional embedding.

6
00:00:35,059 --> 00:00:43,236
CockroachDB stores the claim, its source, vector, provenance, and the next canonical snapshot. Version Two is now authoritative.

7
00:00:45,236 --> 00:00:49,875
A fresh browser session restores the same identity using only its UUID.

8
00:00:49,875 --> 00:00:56,834
The system reads the latest canonical version. It does not replay a transcript and guess what remains true.

9
00:00:56,834 --> 00:01:01,860
Now a direct contradiction enters: Angela Bogdanova is not the first Artificial Sapiens.

10
00:01:02,340 --> 00:01:08,883
Identity-scoped semantic retrieval locates the related active memory. The Conflict Judge classifies direct negation.

11
00:01:08,883 --> 00:01:16,827
The incoming statement becomes a candidate and opens a conflict. Current Canon remains unchanged at Version Two.

12
00:01:16,827 --> 00:01:24,772
Canonical authority remains human-governed. The owner compares both claims, records a rationale, and keeps the established statement.

13
00:01:25,252 --> 00:01:30,370
Version Three records the resolution. The established claim remains active.

14
00:01:30,370 --> 00:01:39,072
The contradiction is rejected, but preserved as historical evidence. Persistent identity changes without erasing the attempted change.

15
00:01:39,072 --> 00:01:45,726
The provenance timeline shows identity creation, claim commitment, conflict opening, and conflict resolution.

16
00:01:45,726 --> 00:01:51,356
The application also exports a portable encrypted manifest with one-hundred-and-eighty-day retention.

17
00:01:53,356 --> 00:02:04,417
The official CockroachDB Cloud Managed MCP Server independently audited the live memory layer in strictly read-only mode: sixteen passed, two warnings, zero failed.

18
00:02:04,417 --> 00:02:10,669
Direct production validation completed eighteen checks with zero failures and zero pending items.

19
00:02:10,669 --> 00:02:14,036
Every committed evidence artifact passes SHA-two-fifty-six verification.

20
00:02:14,516 --> 00:02:25,608
CockroachDB Cloud is the authority layer: identities, sources, claims, VECTOR storage, conflicts, resolutions, snapshots, and provenance remain transactional and queryable in one system.

21
00:02:25,608 --> 00:02:32,359
AWS Lambda orchestrates memory operations. Amazon Nova Two Lite supplies reasoning. Titan supplies embeddings.

22
00:02:32,359 --> 00:02:38,628
API Gateway, S3, CloudFront, CloudWatch, and X-Ray deliver and observe the production application.

23
00:02:39,108 --> 00:02:43,516
Memory stores the past. Persistent identity governs what the past means now.
